	(text "EXT_ORIENT=1: CC1 / TX1 / RX1. EXT_ORIENT=0: CC2 / TX2 / RX2. Set it from the CC that carries the host's Rp.\nThe host transmitters carry the RX1/RX2 AC coupling; the hub upstream capacitors cover TX1/TX2.\nTX1/TX2 are swapped against the receptacle on purpose: USB 3 receivers correct lane polarity.\nRear D+/D- reach the hub through the host mux (SEL_EXT) or the CM5 USB OTG port through U906 (SEL_CM5).\nHUB_UP_VBUS = (CM5_USB_VBUS_EN AND SEL_CM5) OR EXT_LINK, about 3.05V after the BAT54C."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 101.6 165.1 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "1257ce11-fc47-45a4-8231-e4ab18f89083")
	)
	(text "CC / USB 2 protection and sink PD"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 25.4 184.15 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.778 1.778)
				(bold yes)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "22a14661-011b-453e-83da-43ff025509ec")
	)
	(text "Host port — front USB-C to an external computer"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 25.4 22.86 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2.54 2.54)
				(bold yes)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "39cc7981-f994-4fc8-9cae-42d29e326b6d")
	)
	(text "RPD_G1/G2 tie to C_CC1/C_CC2: the dead-battery Rd asks an unpowered host port for VBUS.\nThe FUSB302B keeps its Rd and is polled on TCA9548 channel 5; INT_N has a pull-up only. VCONN is unused.\nFLT is open: a sink cannot remove the host's VBUS, and the TPD6S300A isolates CC and D+/D- itself.\nD1/D2 stay grounded: they are 6V clamps and would void the 24V short protection D+/D- get through C_SBU1/2."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 25.4 274.32 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "8efba526-65ad-4150-b774-13b99d79b175")
	)
